{"id":"DRKS00034406","src":"drks","title":"Non-interventional, prospective, multicenter study to evaluate treatment satisfaction, treatment preference, quality of life, and tolerability under treatment with Briumvi® for relapsing forms of multiple sclerosis (RMS) with active disease in daily clinical practice","official":"","summary":"The main objective of this study is to investigate how satisfied patients are with their treatment and whether they can confirm their decision for this therapy after one or two years of treatment. Furthermore, it is planned to investigate the duration of treatment and what effects the treatment has on the quality of life, and your health status. A total of 600 patients from around 80 clinics and neurological specialist practices are planned to take part in the study.","conditions":["Multiple sclerosis"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"RMS patients with active disease who are treated with newly prescribed Briumvi® (ublituximab) in routine clinical practice  are enrolled after successful review of eligibility criteria and written informed consent during a routine visit. Treating physicians will be instructed to follow their standar"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n- Established clinical diagnosis of RMS with active disease.\r\n- Having been prescribed treatment with Briumvi® according to label and treatment is already initiated, with enrollment occurring no more than 90 days after the first dose.\r\nOR:\r\nPatient with newly prescribed Briumvi® in accordance with the label and about to start treatment with Briumvi® at Visit 1.\r\n- Ability to understand the purpose and risks of the study and willing to provide signed and dated study-specific ICF.\nExclusion criteria:\nPatient cannot be regularly followed up for organizational or geographic reasons.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2024-06-14","pcd":"2028-07-31","upd":"2026-05-18","sp